  "notes": [
    {
      "title": "Startup gates and failure",
      "text": "A live handle is returned with no new spawn. Missing account → NOT_FOUND; empty → NEEDS_LOGIN. Supervisor errors (e.g. KEY_UNAVAILABLE) go to the error file; exit or 60s → INTERNAL.",
      "source": "src/session.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "Autosave is best-effort",
      "text": "Every 30s (configurable, 0 = off), on SIGUSR2 (crumb sync) and SIGTERM/SIGINT it saves a merged snapshot; errors are only logged. Closing the window exits with no final save.",
      "source": "src/session.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "Unauthenticated CDP port",
      "text": "Chrome runs with --remote-debugging-port on 127.0.0.1, and the handle stores its http/ws URLs. Any local process that can reach the port can drive the logged-in browser.",
      "source": "src/browser.ts"
    }
  ],
